03F6                             ; `, ( n -- r ). The seed goes one step on: seed * 261 + 1, which takes
03F6                             ; every 16-bit value in turn. The high bits of such a seed are the good ones
03F6                             ; and the low ones repeat soon, so the high byte is folded into the low
03F6                             ; (XOR) before the remainder of dividing by n is taken.
