0493                             ; skip: read past text to the closer at this level, and return A = 0 if it
0493                             ; was ")" and 2 if it was "]". Brackets of both kinds count together;
0493                             ; strings are stepped over whole. A NUL first ends the program (for "\" with
0493                             ; no closer; anything else that runs into the NUL had unbalanced brackets
0493                             ; anyway). D counts the open levels, starting at 1 for the one we are in:
0493                             ; skip sets it to 0 and falls through the INR that an opener comes back to.
0493                             ; 
0493                             ; The checked build also looks at the character the skip was started by,
0493                             ; which is always the one just before where it starts: "(" must end at ")",
0493                             ; "[" at "]", and neither may run into the NUL (N); a string with no closing
0493                             ; quote counts as running into it. "\" takes either closer. The place where
0493                             ; the skip started is kept on the stack, for the report.
