04FD                             ; =============================================================================
04FD                             ;  Console layer. rawk is the host's key routine: a waiting key in A (zero
04FD                             ;  flag clear), or A = 0 with the zero flag set when none is waiting. putc
04FD                             ;  (RST 5) prints A. Both keep BC, DE and HL. In the generic build they are
04FD                             ;  the host's KEY and CONOUT routines themselves.
04FD                             ; 
04FD                             ;  A running program reads the keyboard only through getk and pollk, which
04FD                             ;  between them give the break key its rules:
04FD                             ;    - Ctrl-C stops the program;
04FD                             ;    - any other key that the break check reads is held in KEYBUF for the
04FD                             ;      next "?", and a newer one takes its place;
04FD                             ;    - "?" (getk) takes the held key first;
04FD                             ;    - a program that has stored a non-zero byte at BRKOFF gets Ctrl-C as a
04FD                             ;      key like any other, but two of them within about 250 ms still stop it.
04FD                             ;  Both are called straight from a handler, never from a routine under one:
04FD                             ;  the checked build's report counts on finding one return address above the
04FD                             ;  data stack, and TOS in HL.
04FD                             ; =============================================================================
04FD                          IFN   CPM   
                    RAWK:     EQU   KEY   
04FD                          ENDIF      
04FD                             ; pollk: the break check (see rpushd).
04FD   CD 40 05     POLLK:    CALL   rawk   
0500   C8                     RZ      ; no key
0501   32 7A 0A               STA   KEYBUF   ; held for the next "?"
0504   FE 03        PK1:      CPI   3   ; (getk joins here)
0506   C0                     RNZ      
0507                             ; ctlc: Ctrl-C has been read. If the break key is on, that is the end. If
0507                             ; the program has turned it off, wait about 250 ms for one more key: a
0507                             ; second Ctrl-C is the end too; any other key is held (the newest wins),
0507                             ; and the Ctrl-C goes to the program: returns A = 3, zero flag clear.
0507   3A 7B 0A     CTLC:     LDA   BRKOFF   
050A   B7                     ORA   A   
050B   CA 82 05               JZ   brk   
050E   D5                     PUSH   D   
050F   11 10 27               LXI   D,250*MSLOOP   
0512   CD 40 05     CT1:      CALL   rawk   
0515   C2 1E 05               JNZ   ct2   
0518   1B                     DCX   D   
0519   7A                     MOV   A,D   
051A   B3                     ORA   E   
051B   C2 12 05               JNZ   ct1   
051E   D1           CT2:      POP   D   ; A = the second key, or 0 if none came
051F   FE 03                  CPI   3   
0521   CA 82 05               JZ   brk   
0524   B7                     ORA   A   
0525   CA 2B 05               JZ   ct3   
0528   32 7A 0A               STA   KEYBUF   
052B   3E 03        CT3:      MVI   A,3   
052D   B7                     ORA   A   
052E   C9                     RET      
052F                             ; getk: a key for "?", or A = 0 and the zero flag if there is none.
052F   E5           GETK:     PUSH   H   ; a held key goes first, and is taken out of
0530   21 7A 0A               LXI   H,KEYBUF   ;   the buffer
0533   7E                     MOV   A,M   
0534   36 00                  MVI   M,0   
0536   E1                     POP   H   
0537   B7                     ORA   A   
0538   C0                     RNZ      
0539   CD 40 05               CALL   rawk   
053C   C8                     RZ      
053D   C3 04 05               JMP   pk1   ; Ctrl-C? If not, that is the key
0540                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                    BRK:      EQU   endprog   ; the unchecked build stops without a word;
0540                          ENDIF      
0540                          IF   CHECKED   
0540                BRK:      EQU   e_break   ;   the checked build reports B
0540                          ENDIF      
0540                          IF   CPM   
0540   3E FF        RAWK:     MVI   A,0FFh   ; BDOS 6 with E = FFh: a key, or 0
0542                             ; putc: BDOS 6 for every character. BDOS 2 would check for ^S while
0542                             ; printing and could swallow a key that BDOS 6 then never sees.
0542   C5           PUTC:     PUSH   B   
0543   D5                     PUSH   D   
0544   E5                     PUSH   H   
0545   5F                     MOV   E,A   
0546   0E 06                  MVI   C,6   
0548   CD 05 00               CALL   BDOS   
054B   E1                     POP   H   
054C   D1                     POP   D   
054D   C1                     POP   B   
054E   B7                     ORA   A   ; (for getk)
054F   C9                     RET      
0550                          ENDIF      
